WEBVTT

00:00:00.604 --> 00:00:04.250
In this show-and-tell we will create two regular Fidelity

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.130
portfolios add them to an Owner account create a

00:00:08.143 --> 00:00:12.831
separate aggregate portfolio and import example Fidelity positions and

00:00:12.844 --> 00:00:16.841
transactions We will start on the Portfolios screen where

00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:20.565
every portfolio begins as its own regular account

00:00:22.317 --> 00:00:25.833
From anywhere in the application open Admin and choose

00:00:25.846 --> 00:00:30.716
Portfolios This screen is where you create select organize

00:00:30.872 --> 00:00:35.677
and import into individual accounts A regular portfolio represents

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.971
one real brokerage or manual account It is the

00:00:38.984 --> 00:00:43.658
account that owns its own holdings cash transactions and

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:44.726
import history

00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:49.391
Owner is an optional personal rollup Think of it

00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:52.203
as the combined view of the real accounts that

00:00:52.216 --> 00:00:56.110
belong to one owner You create Owner once then

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.961
use the Owner column to choose its member accounts

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:02.438
Owner adds those accounts together for viewing it does

00:01:02.438 --> 00:01:05.563
not replace them and it has no broker file

00:01:05.563 --> 00:01:09.703
of its own Continue importing positions and transactions into

00:01:09.873 --> 00:01:13.505
each regular account and Owner reflects the combined result

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:18.926
Here are the two regular demo accounts Fidelity Income

00:01:18.926 --> 00:01:22.819
Demo and Fidelity Activity Demo To make each one

00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:27.650
choose New Portfolio enter a descriptive account name select

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:30.749
Fidelity as the broker source and save it as

00:01:30.762 --> 00:01:33.496
a user-owned account Then check the Owner box for

00:01:33.614 --> 00:01:36.712
each account you want included In this example both

00:01:36.712 --> 00:01:40.710
Fidelity portfolios are members so Owner shows their combined

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.887
data while each remains an independent portfolio

00:01:45.644 --> 00:01:49.485
A regular aggregate portfolio is different from Owner It

00:01:49.485 --> 00:01:52.441
is a read-only virtual view that you name and

00:01:52.441 --> 00:01:57.415
define by selecting any regular portfolios Here Demo Fidelity

00:01:57.415 --> 00:02:01.100
Aggregate contains the two Fidelity demos It does not

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.394
move data or change either account You can create

00:02:04.394 --> 00:02:07.910
as many aggregates as you need for any comparison

00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:11.569
or grouping and the same regular portfolio can belong

00:02:11.582 --> 00:02:13.717
to more than one aggregate at the same time

00:02:15.506 --> 00:02:19.452
For a Fidelity account select the destination portfolio first

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.892
open Import Portfolio Data choose Broker Import and start

00:02:23.905 --> 00:02:28.293
with Step 1 Positions Select Fidelity and upload the

00:02:28.293 --> 00:02:34.816
renamed fidelity_positions_Demo spreadsheet A positions file establishes the current

00:02:34.816 --> 00:02:38.592
holdings and cash snapshot so it should normally be

00:02:38.592 --> 00:02:40.832
imported before transaction history

00:02:42.574 --> 00:02:46.116
Always use Preview before importing The preview confirms the

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:49.697
file account and the selected destination then shows the

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:53.421
holdings cash and total account value it found In

00:02:53.421 --> 00:02:58.486
this demo the Fidelity snapshot identifies two securities plus

00:02:58.486 --> 00:03:02.874
cash Check those results against the exported statement then

00:03:03.004 --> 00:03:07.913
choose Import into Fidelity Income Demo The completed import

00:03:07.926 --> 00:03:10.087
reports two new positions

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:16.157
Next select Fidelity Activity Demo and choose Step 2

00:03:16.457 --> 00:03:21.821
Transactions Transaction files add buys sells dividends and DRIP

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:25.207
activity The application warns when there is no current

00:03:25.207 --> 00:03:29.061
positions snapshot because a partial history can rebuild the

00:03:29.061 --> 00:03:33.149
wrong share counts In this controlled demonstration the supplied

00:03:33.149 --> 00:03:36.548
file is complete sample history so we acknowledge the

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:41.600
confirmation In normal use import positions first then add

00:03:41.613 --> 00:03:43.436
the full transaction export

00:03:45.174 --> 00:03:48.989
Preview the transaction spreadsheet and verify the activity types

00:03:49.198 --> 00:03:54.953
dates tickers quantities and destination portfolio This Fidelity example

00:03:54.953 --> 00:03:59.263
finds two buys one dividend and one DRIP reinvestment

00:03:59.692 --> 00:04:02.948
When the preview matches the export import it into

00:04:02.948 --> 00:04:07.427
Fidelity Activity Demo The confirmation shows the activity that

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:11.060
was added while Owner and the Demo Fidelity Aggregate

00:04:11.073 --> 00:04:14.289
remain combined views of their chosen regular accounts

00:04:16.001 --> 00:04:19.764
To recap create a regular portfolio for every real

00:04:19.764 --> 00:04:23.384
account and import directly into it Use the optional

00:04:23.397 --> 00:04:26.522
Owner account when you want one personal rollup of

00:04:26.535 --> 00:04:30.884
selected user-owned accounts Use regular aggregates for any other

00:04:30.897 --> 00:04:34.881
virtual grouping You can have many aggregates reuse accounts

00:04:34.881 --> 00:04:37.889
across them and change their members without changing the

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:42.433
original account data For informational purposes only Not financial

00:04:42.433 --> 00:04:43.032
advice
